  "evidence_text": "Page: Slam Creepers. Sentence: Slam Creepers were a rock band from Vansbro, Sweden formed by Björn Skifs in 1962 and broke up in 1969.\nPage: Slam Creepers. Sentence: Skifs would later find success with a number 1 hit \"Hooked on a Feeling as a member of Blue Swede.\nPage: Hooked on a Feeling. Sentence: “Hooked on a Feeling” is a 1968 pop song written by Mark James and originally performed by B. J. Thomas.\nPage: Hooked on a Feeling. Sentence: The Blue Swede version made singer Björn Skifs' \"Ooga-Chaka-Ooga-Ooga\" intro well known (and famous in Sweden at the time), although it had been used originally by British musician Jonathan King in his 1971 version of the song.",
