  "grafo_evidencia": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "02680b92-aaa5-52c1-8595-d3715aca27e2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Björn Skifs, Mark James, B. J. Thomas, Jonathan King\n- Music groups: Slam Creepers, Blue Swede\n- Places: Vansbro, Sweden\n- Songs: “Hooked on a Feeling”\n\nFacts:\n- Slam Creepers were a rock band from Vansbro, Sweden, formed by Björn Skifs in 1962.\n- “Hooked on a Feeling” is a 1968 pop song written by Mark James and originally performed by B. J. Thomas.\n- Slam Creepers broke up in 1969.\n- Jonathan King used the “Ooga-Chaka-Ooga-Ooga” intro in his 1971 version of “Hooked on a Feeling.”\n- Björn Skifs later found success as a member of Blue Swede with a number 1 hit version of “Hooked on a Feeling.”\n- Blue Swede’s version of “Hooked on a Feeling” made Björn Skifs’ “Ooga-Chaka-Ooga-Ooga” intro well known and famous in Sweden at the time.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "adf7b8df-a3d9-5959-bd76-8837de92b127",
        "text": "Page: Slam Creepers. Sentence: Slam Creepers were a rock band from Vansbro, Sweden formed by Björn Skifs in 1962 and broke up in 1969.\nPage: Slam Creepers. Sentence: Skifs would later find success with a number 1 hit \"Hooked on a Feeling as a member of Blue Swede.\nPage: Hooked on a Feeling. Sentence: “Hooked on a Feeling” is a 1968 pop song written by Mark James and originally performed by B. J. Thomas.\nPage: Hooked on a Feeling. Sentence: The Blue Swede version made singer Björn Skifs' \"Ooga-Chaka-Ooga-Ooga\" intro well known (and famous in Sweden at the time), although it had been used originally by British musician Jonathan King in his 1971 version of the song.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
